    "bbf3a91b-f594-47df-879a-1171c37568cc": "{\"id\": \"bbf3a91b-f594-47df-879a-1171c37568cc\", \"title\": \"Understanding eCourts System Basics\", \"created_at\": \"2026-03-11T08:42:37.320652\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-11T10:27:44.049830\", \"user_id\": 5, \"generated\": [\"Aapne eCourts ke baare mein puchha hai. eCourts Bharat ke nyayik pranali mein ek mahatvapoorn sangathan hai. Yeh ek online portal hai jahan se aap apne nyayik kaam kar sakte hain, jaise ki FIR daalna, case track karna, aur adhikarik kagazat download karna.\\n\\neCourts ke dwara, aap apne ghar se hi nyayik kaam kar sakte hain aur samay aur paise bacha sakte hain. Yeh portal National Judicial Data Grid (NJDG) ke madhyam se nyayik data ko eekrshan karta hai aur nyayik kaam ko swasthikrit karta hai.\\n\\nAap eCourts ki official website par ja sakte hain: [www. ecourts. gov. in](http://www. ecourts. gov. in). Yahaan se aap apne nyayik kaam karne ke liye online form bhar sakte hain aur apne case ke updates dekh sakte hain.\", \"You're asking about eCourts. eCourts is a crucial institution in India's judicial system. It's an online portal where you can carry out judicial work from the comfort of your home, such as filing an FIR, tracking cases, and downloading official documents.\\n\\nWith eCourts, you can save time and money by carrying out judicial work online. The portal uses the National Judicial Data Grid (NJDG) to digitize judicial data and ensure the integrity of judicial work.\\n\\nYou can visit the official eCourts website at: [www. ecourts. gov. in](http://www. ecourts. gov. in). From there, you can fill out online forms and track updates on your case.\\n\\nFor more information on eCourts, you can also visit the official website of the Ministry of Law and Justice: [www. moj. gov. moj. gov. in).\", \"The Supreme Court of India has a total of 34 judges, including the Chief Justice of India. However, the strength of the Supreme Court can vary as judges retire or are appointed. According to the Supreme Court's official website, the current sanctioned strength of judges is 34, but the actual number of working judges may be less due to various reasons such as leave or temporary assignments.\\n\\nYou can find more information on the Supreme Court's judges and their profiles on the official website of the Supreme Court of India: [www. sc. nic. in](http://www. sc. nic. in).\", \"The Indian Penal Code (IPC) is a comprehensive code that defines various offenses and prescribes punishments for them. It was enacted in 1860 and is one of the oldest and most widely used penal codes in the world. The IPC consists of 23 chapters and 511 sections, covering a wide range of topics such as crimes against the state, crimes against the person, and crimes against property.\\n\\nThe IPC is a crucial piece of legislation that helps maintain law and order in India. It provides a framework for the criminal justice system and ensures that offenders are held accountable for their actions.\\n\\nYou can find more information on the IPC on the official website of the Ministry of Law and Justice: [www. moj. gov. in](http://www. moj. gov. in).\"], \"past\": [\"Do you know about ecourts\", \"rply with english\", \"how many judges in supreme court\", \"What is IPC\"], \"source\": [\"GEN\", \"GEN\", \"GEN\", \"GEN_CORRECTED\"]}",
