    "5d9d1789-7e87-4dcb-9546-07d2d08fa157": "{\"id\": \"5d9d1789-7e87-4dcb-9546-07d2d08fa157\", \"title\": \"New Chat\", \"created_at\": \"2026-03-11T11:28:00.164252\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-11T11:28:00.164288\", \"user_id\": \"6eb1c649-a1cd-4847-905c-e082d342ebe8\", \"generated\": [], \"past\": [], \"source\": []}",
    "0c3af8e1-c6b4-4cd7-b018-25270953579f": "{\"id\": \"0c3af8e1-c6b4-4cd7-b018-25270953579f\", \"title\": \"Introduction to Integrated Circuits\", \"created_at\": \"2026-03-11T12:07:32.409340\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-11T12:09:22.347706\", \"user_id\": 8, \"generated\": [\"Bharatiya Dand Sanhita, jise aam taur par IPC ke naam se jaana jata hai, Bharat mein dandon ka sanhita hai. Iska purana naam Indian Penal Code tha. Yeh 1860 mein banaya gaya tha aur ismein Bharat mein kai dandon ki suchi hai, jaise ki hatya, loot, aur anya ghatnayein.\", \"The Indian Penal Code, commonly referred to as IPC, is the main criminal code of India. It was established in 1860 and contains a list of various offenses, such as murder, theft, and other crimes.\"], \"past\": [\"What is IPC?\", \"in english\"], \"source\": [\"HYBRID_GRAPH\", \"GEN\"]}",
    "0fc71498-fccd-49f2-b2a2-d43de973e02e": "{\"id\": \"0fc71498-fccd-49f2-b2a2-d43de973e02e\", \"title\": \"eCourts Online Case Management\", \"created_at\": \"2026-03-15T15:37:27.716192\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-15T17:22:55.363261\", \"user_id\": \"c0080518-6d3a-469f-8141-42d5a10ce971\", \"generated\": [\"Namaskaram! eCourts ek online portal hai jahan se aap court ke records, case status, aur kai anya jaankari prapt kar sakte hain. Iske madhyam se aap court ke proceedings, case files, aur judgements online dekh sakte hain. Aapko inke liye cybercrime. gov. in ya ecourts. gov. in par jaakar jaankari prapt kar sakti hai.\", \"### 1. Relevant Section(s) & Act(s) - Section 304, Part II (Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, BNS) / Section 304, Part II (Indian Penal Code, IPC) - Section 338 (Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, BNS) / Section 338 (Indian Penal Code, IPC) ### 2. Legal Explanation Murder ase (culpable homicide not amounting to murder) aur section 304, Part II ke sandarbhe mein, yadi koi vyakti apne galtiyon se jaan-bachao ke liye khatre mein padta hai ya kisi ke jaan-bachao ke liye khatre mein padta hai, to iske liye section 304, Part II ka aayogya hoga.\", \"Namaste! Aap kya chaahte hain?\", \"Main Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS) aur Indian Penal Code (IPC) ke sandarbhe mein aapko sahi jaankari pradan karta hoon. Main aapko ismein sahayata karne ke liye upalabdh hoon.\", \"I'm a Legal Information and Guidance Assistant, created by the Department of Justice to provide accurate and clear explanations of Indian laws, including the Indian Penal Code (IPC), Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), and other relevant acts. My purpose is to assist citizens in understanding their rights and responsibilities under the law.\\n\\nI'm a machine learning model, trained on a vast amount of legal data and information. I'm designed to provide general educational summaries and guidance on various legal topics, but I'm not a substitute for a qualified legal professional. If you have specific questions or concerns, I encourage you to consult a lawyer or visit the nearest Legal Aid Clinic for personalized advice.\\n\\nYou can find more information about the Department of Justice and its initiatives on the official website: [www. doj. gov. in](http://www. doj. gov. in).\"], \"past\": [\"Hello!Do you know about eCourts?\", \"hi do you know about murder ase and section\", \"hi\", \"hi whats you doing for DOJ\", \"Hello!Who are you?I didnt know about you when you are created?\"], \"source\": [\"GEN\", \"HYBRID_GRAPH\", \"GEN\", \"GEN\", \"GEN\"]}",
    "test_chat_123": "{\"id\": \"test_chat_123\", \"title\": \"Understanding eCourts System Basics\", \"created_at\": \"2026-03-15T15:43:29.252415\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-15T15:44:14.751158\", \"generated\": [\"Namaste! eCourts is a pioneering initiative by the Indian government to provide online access to court services and case information. It aims to increase transparency, efficiency, and citizen engagement with the judiciary. You can visit the official eCourts website at [ecourts. gov. in](http://ecourts. gov. in) to learn more about its features and services.\\n\\neCourts is a significant step towards digitalizing the Indian judiciary and making it more accessible to citizens.\"], \"past\": [\"Hello!Do you know about eCourts?\"], \"source\": [\"GEN\"], \"user_id\": null}",
    "test_chat_lang": "{\"id\": \"test_chat_lang\", \"title\": \"Hello How Are You\", \"created_at\": \"2026-03-15T17:11:55.763681\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-15T17:13:02.061899\", \"generated\": [\"Hello! How can I assist you with Indian legal information today?\", \"### 1.\\n\\n### 2.\\nSection 302 IPC deals with punishment for murder. It states that whoever commits murder shall be punished with death or imprisonment for life, and also be liable to fine. The key elements to prove murder under this section are the intention to cause death, the actual cause of death, and the absence of any legal justification for the act.\\n\\n### 3.\\nThe punishment for murder under Section 302 IPC can be death or imprisonment for life, along with a fine.\\n\\n### 4.\\nTo file a case under Section 302 IPC, the victim's family or the police can file an FIR at the nearest police station. The case will then be investigated and charges will be framed under Section 302 IPC. The trial will take place in a court of law, and the accused will be entitled to a fair trial.\\n\\n### 5.\\nIf you are a victim of a murder or have information about a murder, please file an FIR at the nearest police station (ecourts. gov. in or cybercrime. gov. in for online filing) and consult a lawyer for guidance.\", \"\\u0928\\u092e\\u0938\\u094d\\u0924\\u0947! \\u0906\\u091c \\u0906\\u092a \\u092e\\u0941\\u091d\\u0938\\u0947 \\u092d\\u093e\\u0930\\u0924\\u0940\\u092f \\u0915\\u093e\\u0928\\u0942\\u0928\\u0940 \\u091c\\u093e\\u0928\\u0915\\u093e\\u0930\\u0940 \\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 \\u0938\\u0939\\u093e\\u092f\\u0924\\u093e \\u091a\\u093e\\u0939\\u0924\\u0947 \\u0939\\u0948\\u0902? \\u0915\\u0943\\u092a\\u092f\\u093e \\u0905\\u092a\\u0928\\u093e \\u092a\\u094d\\u0930\\u0936\\u094d\\u0928 \\u092a\\u0942\\u091b\\u0947\\u0902 \\u0924\\u093e\\u0915\\u093f \\u092e\\u0948\\u0902 \\u0906\\u092a\\u0915\\u0940 \\u0938\\u0939\\u093e\\u092f\\u0924\\u093e \\u0915\\u0930 \\u0938\\u0915\\u0942\\u0901\\u0964\", \"\\u0bb5\\u0ba3\\u0b95\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bae\\u0bcd! \\u0ba8\\u0bc0\\u0b99\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bb3\\u0bcd \\u0b87\\u0ba8\\u0bcd\\u0ba4\\u0bbf\\u0baf \\u0b9a\\u0b9f\\u0bcd\\u0b9f\\u0ba4\\u0bcd\\u0ba4\\u0bbf\\u0bb2\\u0bcd \\u0baa\\u0bb1\\u0bcd\\u0bb1\\u0bbf\\u0baf \\u0b95\\u0bc7\\u0bb3\\u0bcd\\u0bb5\\u0bbf\\u0b95\\u0bb3\\u0bc8\\u0b95\\u0bcd \\u0b95\\u0bc7\\u0b9f\\u0bcd\\u0b9f\\u0bc1\\u0b95\\u0bcd \\u0b95\\u0bca\\u0bb3\\u0bcd\\u0bb5\\u0ba4\\u0bb1\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bc1 \\u0bb5\\u0bb0\\u0bc1\\u0b95\\u0bbf\\u0bb1\\u0bc0\\u0bb0\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bb3\\u0bbe? \\u0ba8\\u0bbe\\u0ba9\\u0bcd \\u0b89\\u0b99\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bb3\\u0bc1\\u0b95\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bc1 \\u0b89\\u0ba4\\u0bb5 \\u0bb5\\u0bc7\\u0ba3\\u0bcd\\u0b9f\\u0bc1\\u0bae\\u0bcd \\u0b8e\\u0ba9\\u0bcd\\u0bb1\\u0bbe\\u0bb2\\u0bcd \\u0baa\\u0bbe\\u0bb0\\u0bcd\\u0ba4\\u0bcd\\u0ba4\\u0bc1\\u0b95\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bca\\u0bb3\\u0bcd\\u0bb3\\u0bc1\\u0b99\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bb3\\u0bcd.\"], \"past\": [\"hi\", \"hi do you know about murder case and section\", \"\\u0928\\u092e\\u0938\\u094d\\u0924\\u0947\", \"\\u0bb5\\u0ba3\\u0b95\\u0bcd\\u0b95\\u0bae\\u0bcd\"], \"source\": [\"GEN\", \"HYBRID_GRAPH\", \"GEN\", \"GEN\"], \"user_id\": null}",
    "47244f49-53b6-4c47-bd90-604c3f860921": "{\"id\": \"47244f49-53b6-4c47-bd90-604c3f860921\", \"title\": \"Karur Stampede Tragic Event History\", \"created_at\": \"2026-03-16T11:53:50.088786\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-16T11:58:17.351894\", \"user_id\": \"555f072b-f873-43c5-8c22-0f9f4148894f\", \"generated\": [\"The Karur Stampede was a tragic incident that occurred in 2000 at the Karur Town Railway Station in Tamil Nadu, India. It was a result of a sudden rush of people during a festival, leading to a stampede that claimed the lives of 36 people and injured many more.\\n\\nUnder Indian law, such incidents are often investigated by the authorities to determine the cause and responsibility behind the tragedy. The Railways Act, 1989, and the Indian Railways (Amendment) Act, 2003, govern the safety and security of railway stations and trains in India.\\n\\nIf you're looking for information on the investigation or the laws related to railway safety, I recommend visiting the official website of the Ministry of Railways (indianrailways. gov. in) or the National Human Rights Commission (nhrc. nic. in). These websites provide detailed information on railway safety regulations and the laws governing such incidents.\\n\\nPlease note that for specific information or guidance on this incident, I would recommend consulting official reports or visiting the nearest Legal Aid Clinic for expert advice.\", \"There is no record of a recent 2025 stampede incident in India that I am aware of. However, I can provide general information on stampede incidents and the laws governing them in India.\\n\\nStampede incidents are often investigated by the authorities to determine the cause and responsibility behind the tragedy. The Railways Act, 1989, and the Indian Railways (Amendment) Act, 2003, govern the safety and security of railway stations and trains in India.\\n\\nIf you're looking for information on stampede incidents or the laws related to public safety, I recommend visiting the official website of the Ministry of Railways (indianrailways. gov. in) or the National Human Rights Commission (nhrc. nic. in). These websites provide detailed information on safety regulations and the laws governing such incidents.\\n\\nPlease note that for specific information or guidance on a particular incident, I would recommend consulting official reports or visiting the nearest Legal Aid Clinic for expert advice.\"], \"past\": [\"Hi! Do you know about Karur Stampede?\", \"recent 2025 stmapede?\"], \"source\": [\"GEN\", \"GEN\"]}",
    "985d0959-6402-4d06-ab9c-cae9f22f7b94": "{\"id\": \"985d0959-6402-4d06-ab9c-cae9f22f7b94\", \"title\": \"Virtual Justice Access Portal\", \"created_at\": \"2026-03-16T20:30:54.910006\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-16T20:31:39.665578\", \"user_id\": \"fa79426b-07e7-42f5-81db-7e80626899e8\", \"generated\": [\"The Tele-Law Service is an innovative initiative by the Department of Justice, Government of India, to provide free legal advice to citizens, especially those from rural and underserved areas. This service is available through a network of Common Service Centers (CSCs) and can be accessed by dialing a toll-free number.\\n\\nTo access the Tele-Law Service, you can visit the official website at [telelaw. gov. in](http://telelaw. gov. in) or contact the nearest CSC. The service is available in multiple languages, including Hindi, English, and several regional languages. A panel of empaneled lawyers provides legal advice on various topics, including family law, property law, and consumer rights.\\n\\nThe Tele-Law Service aims to increase access to justice and provide citizens with a platform to seek legal advice from the comfort of their homes. It's a great resource for those who cannot afford to hire a lawyer or are not aware of their legal rights.\\n\\nFor more information, you can visit the official website or contact the National Legal Services Authority (NALSA) at [nalsa. gov. in](http://nalsa. gov. in).\"], \"past\": [\"Tele-Law Service\"], \"source\": [\"GEN\"]}",
    "verification_chat_123": "{\"id\": \"verification_chat_123\", \"title\": \"Registering a FIR for Theft\", \"created_at\": \"2026-03-17T10:49:11.629597\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-17T10:52:11.116839\", \"generated\": [\"### 1. Relevant Section(s) & Act(s) To register a First Information Report (FIR) for theft, the relevant sections under Indian law are: * Section 379 of the Indian Penal Code (IPC), which deals with punishment for theft. * Section 154 of the Code of Criminal Procedure (CrPC), which deals with the procedure for registering an FIR. ### 2. Legal Explanation When a theft occurs, the victim or anyone who has knowledge of the theft can report it to the police. The police officer will then record the information provided by the complainant in a book called the General Diary (GD). However, if the police officer is satisfied that a cognizable offense has been committed, they will register an FIR. The FIR is a written document that contains the details of the offense, including the date, time, place, and description of the offense. The FIR is a crucial document that serves as the basis for further investigation. ### 3. Punishment / Penalty Under Section 379 of the IPC, the punishment for theft is imprisonment for up to three years, or a fine, or both. However, the punishment can be more severe if the value of the stolen property exceeds Rs. 1 lakh. ### 4. Legal Procedure To register a FIR for theft, follow these steps: 1. **Visit the nearest police station**: Go to the police station in your area and report the theft to the police officer on duty. 2. **Provide information**: Provide the police officer with as much information as possible about the theft, including the date, time, place, and description of the stolen property. 3. **Fill out the FIR**: The police officer will fill out the FIR based on the information provided by the complainant. 4. **Get a copy of the FIR**: Once the FIR is registered, the police officer will provide a copy of the FIR to the complainant. 5. **Preserve evidence**: Preserve any evidence related to the theft, such as CCTV footage, witness statements, and photographs of the stolen property. ### 5.\", \"The Legal Services Authorities Act, 1987, provides free legal services to the economically weaker sections of the society. The Act establishes a network of legal services authorities at the national, state, and district levels to provide legal aid to the needy.\\n\\nYou can approach the Legal Services Authorities in your state or district to seek legal aid.\\n\\n1. **Identify the Legal Services Authority**: Find the Legal Services Authority in your state or district. You can search online or check the official website of the National Legal Services Authority (NALSA) for contact details.\\n2. **Visit the Legal Services Authority**: Visit the Legal Services Authority in person or write to them to seek legal aid. You can also contact them through their helpline numbers.\\n3. **Provide necessary documents**: Provide the necessary documents, such as your income certificate, caste certificate, and identity proof, to the Legal Services Authority.\\n4. **Meet with a lawyer**: The Legal Services Authority will assign a lawyer to meet with you and discuss your case. The lawyer will provide you with free legal advice and represent you in court if necessary.\\n5. **Get a legal aid card**: If you are eligible for legal aid, you will be issued a legal aid card. This card will entitle you to free legal services from a lawyer.\\n\\n* **National Legal Services Authority (NALSA)**: NALSA is the apex body for legal services in India. You can contact NALSA through their website or helpline numbers.\\n* **State Legal Services Authorities**: Each state has its own Legal Services Authority. You can contact the State Legal Services Authority in your state for legal aid.\\n* **District Legal Services Authorities**: Each district has its own Legal Services Authority. You can contact the District Legal Services Authority in your district for legal aid.\\n\\n* National Legal Services Authority (NALSA): [www. nalsa. gov. in](http://www. nalsa. gov.\\n* State Legal Services Authorities: [www. nalsa. gov. in/state-lsa](http://www. nalsa. gov.\\n* District Legal Services Authorities: [www. nalsa. gov. in/dlsa](http://www. nalsa. gov.\\n\\nNote: The above information is based on the Legal Services Authorities Act, 1987, and the rules framed thereunder. The information is subject to change, and you should verify the same with the relevant authorities before seeking legal aid.\", \"eCourts is an online platform that provides access to court-related information and services. It was launched by the Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India, to make the judicial system more transparent and accessible to citizens.\\n\\n* Case status: You can check the status of your case, including the date of hearing, next date of hearing, and the current status of the case.\\n* Court orders: You can view court orders, judgments, and decrees online.\\n* Cause list: You can view the cause list of the court, which includes the list of cases to be heard on a particular date.\\n* Court calendar: You can view the court calendar, which includes the list of cases to be heard in the coming days.\\n\\n1. **Visit the eCourts website**: Go to the eCourts website at [ecourts. gov. in](http://ecourts. gov. in).\\n2. **Select your state**: Select your state from the list of states provided on the website.\\n3. **Select your district**: Select your district from the list of districts provided on the website.\\n4. **Select your court**: Select the court where your case is pending.\\n5. **Enter your case details**: Enter your case details, including the case number, court name, and judge's name.\\n6. **Check your case status**: Click on the \\\"Case Status\\\" button to check the status of your case.\\n\\nYou can also use the eCourts mobile app to check your case status. The app is available for both Android and iOS devices.\\n\\n* **eCourts website**: [ecourts. gov. gov.\"], \"past\": [\"How can I register a FIR for theft? Explain the steps clearly.\", \"What are the steps to get legal aid in India?\", \"What is eCourts and how do I use it to check my case status?\"], \"source\": [\"GEN\", \"GEN\", \"GEN\"], \"user_id\": null}",
    "035b1682-e1d7-4a73-8405-206d5a3e3dfd": "{\"id\": \"035b1682-e1d7-4a73-8405-206d5a3e3dfd\", \"title\": \"New Chat\", \"created_at\": \"2026-03-17T11:29:52.773790\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-17T11:29:52.773849\", \"user_id\": \"2dced8ff-60c3-4871-b83f-57954d9454ae\", \"generated\": [], \"past\": [], \"source\": []}",
    "test_workload_chat": "{\"id\": \"test_workload_chat\", \"title\": \"Understanding Anticipatory Bail Laws\", \"created_at\": \"2026-03-17T12:16:53.026169\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-17T12:16:55.578972\", \"generated\": [\"### 1. Relevant Section(s) & Act(s) Anticipatory bail is governed by Section 438 of the Code of Criminal Procedure (CrPC), 1973, which is part of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS). This section allows a person to apply for anticipatory bail before an arrest is made, if they fear that they might be arrested for a non-bailable offense. ### 2. Legal Explanation (Simplified) Anticipatory bail is a type of bail that is applied for before an arrest is made. This means that a person can apply for bail even before they have been arrested, if they think that they might be arrested for a non-bailable offense. The main purpose of anticipatory bail is to prevent the person from being arrested and put in jail, while their case is being decided. To apply for anticipatory bail, the person must show that they have a genuine reason to fear that they might be arrested, and that they will not run away from the law. The court will consider the seriousness of the offense, the likelihood of the person appearing for trial, and other relevant factors before granting anticipatory bail. ### 3. Punishment / Penalty There is no specific punishment or penalty mentioned in Section 438 of the CrPC for not obtaining anticipatory bail. However, if a person is arrested and they do not have anticipatory bail, they may face arrest and detention in jail until their case is decided. ### 4. Legal Procedure To apply for anticipatory bail, you must follow these steps: 1. **Consult a lawyer**: You should consult a lawyer who is familiar with the law and the court procedures. 2. **Prepare the application**: Your lawyer will help you prepare the application for anticipatory bail, which must be filed in the High Court or the Sessions Court. 3. **File the application**: The application must be filed in the court before the arrest is made. 4. **Court hearing**: The court will hear the application and decide whether to grant anticipatory bail or not. 5. **Grant of bail**: If the court grants anticipatory bail, you will be released from the risk of arrest. ### 5. Recommended Action If you think that you might be arrested for a non-bailable offense, you should: 1.\"], \"past\": [\"What is anticipatory bail?\"], \"source\": [\"JSON_CONCEPT\"], \"user_id\": null}",
    "test_hindi_chat": "{\"id\": \"test_hindi_chat\", \"title\": \"\\u0938\\u0902\\u091c\\u094d\\u091e\\u0947\\u092f \\u0905\\u092a\\u0930\\u093e\\u0927 \\u0915\\u0940 \\u0935\\u093f\\u0936\\u0947\\u0937\\u0924\\u093e\\u090f\\u0901\", \"created_at\": \"2026-03-17T12:24:19.916890\", \"updated_at\": \"2026-03-17T12:24:22.803609\", \"generated\": [\"### 1. Relevant Section(s) & Act(s) \\u0938\\u0902\\u091c\\u094d\\u091e\\u0947\\u092f \\u0905\\u092a\\u0930\\u093e\\u0927 \\u0915\\u0947 \\u0932\\u093f\\u090f \\u092d\\u093e\\u0930\\u0924\\u0940\\u092f \\u0926\\u0902\\u0921 \\u0938\\u0902\\u0939\\u093f\\u0924\\u093e (\\u0906\\u0908\\u092a\\u0940\\u0938\\u0940) \\u0915\\u0940 \\u0927\\u093e\\u0930\\u093e 2(\\u0915) \\u0914\\u0930 \\u092d\\u093e\\u0930\\u0924\\u0940\\u092f \\u0928\\u094d\\u092f\\u093e\\u092f \\u092a\\u094d\\u0930\\u0923\\u093e\\u0932\\u0940 \\u0915\\u0947 \\u0928\\u093f\\u092f\\u092e\\u094b\\u0902 \\u0915\\u093e \\u0938\\u0902\\u0926\\u0930\\u094d\\u092d \\u0932\\u093f\\u092f\\u093e \\u091c\\u093e\\u0924\\u093e \\u0939\\u0948\\u0964 ### 2. Legal Explanation (Simplified) \\u0938\\u0902\\u091c\\u094d\\u091e\\u0947\\u092f \\u0905\\u092a\\u0930\\u093e\\u0927 \\u0935\\u0939 \\u0905\\u092a\\u0930\\u093e\\u0927 \\u0939\\u0948 \\u091c\\u093f\\u0938\\u092e\\u0947\\u0902 \\u092a\\u0941\\u0932\\u093f\\u0938 \\u0915\\u094b \\u0928\\u094d\\u092f\\u093e\\u092f\\u093e\\u0927\\u0940\\u0936 \\u0938\\u0947 \\u0935\\u093e\\u0930\\u0902\\u091f \\u0915\\u093e \\u0907\\u0902\\u0924\\u091c\\u093e\\u0930 \\u0915\\u093f\\u090f \\u092c\\u093f\\u0928\\u093e, \\u0905\\u092a\\u0930\\u093e\\u0927 \\u0915\\u0947 \\u0938\\u0902\\u0926\\u093f\\u0917\\u094d\\u0927 \\u0915\\u093f\\u0938\\u0940 \\u092d\\u0940 \\u0935\\u094d\\u092f\\u0915\\u094d\\u0924\\u093f \\u0915\\u094b \\u0924\\u0941\\u0930\\u0902\\u0924 \\u0917\\u093f\\u0930\\u092b\\u094d\\u0924\\u093e\\u0930 \\u0915\\u0930\\u0928\\u0947 \\u0915\\u093e \\u0905\\u0927\\u093f\\u0915\\u093e\\u0930 \\u0939\\u0948\\u0964 \\u092f\\u0939 \\u0905\